{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLHG8GUwHGTqvtaThrgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01575vykyZi3JShY7ZWe6R8G","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; python3 - <<'E'\nf='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(f).read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nsub(\"| `ard:needs-human` | Controller, from the agent's result |\",\"| `ard:needs-human` | Controller, from the agent's result, or a scanner at filing (`route: needs-human`) |\")\nsub(\"so a half-parsed run can never trigger autoclose. Titles,\",\"so a half-parsed run can never trigger autoclose. Titles,\")\n# paragraph after strict schema: end of line 175 text\na=\"so scanner output cannot forge a marker.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n\n**The pre-filing guard cannot be turned off.** After every scan and before the diff, in dry-run too and even with zero findings, the controller scans the title, fingerprint, group, files and body of every finding with the builtin pattern scanner and the controller's known secret values, plus gitleaks when `redact.gitleaks.enabled`. A hit, a builtin-pass failure or an invalid line changes nothing: no issue is filed, joined, edited, ticked or closed, no finding row is written from the run's findings (reconcile and the dry-run ledger adoption, which read GitHub and the ledger, still run before the scan), and the run is recorded as `scan_failed`. When gitleaks is enabled but cannot run, nothing is filed, joined or edited, but autoclose of already-filed issues still proceeds (an issue is ticked only when it closes) unless `redact.gitleaks.block_autoclose_when_missing: true`; the run is still `scan_failed`. Logs name only the rule and the field of a hit (known values by env var name); a pass failure also logs its error. A shutdown during the guard records no run.\n\n**Route.** The scanner key `route` decides where its issues go: `pending` (default for executable scanners) files with `ard:pending`, so they enter triage; `none` (default for LLM scanners) files with the scanner label only, and a human adds `ard:pending` to send one issue to triage; `needs-human` files with `ard:needs-human` and no `ard:pending`, so no agent triages them. LLM scanners may not use `pending`. Changing `route` affects only new issues. A human promotes one issue by removing `ard:needs-human` and/or adding `ard:pending`; after that ard never joins findings onto it.\"\"\")\nsub(\"it skips the run and logs it, autoclose scanners included:\",\"it skips the run and logs it, autoclose scanners included (`none` and `needs-human` issues count too, and are never stale-closed, so a non-autoclose scanner with those routes stops once its issues fill `max_open` until a human closes or promotes some):\")\nsub(\"it carries no `ard:` label besides `ard:scanner:<name>` and `ard:pending`;\",\"it carries no `ard:` label besides `ard:scanner:<name>` and the route's label (none under `route: none`);\")\nsub(\"Create the issue with `ard:scanner:<name>` and `ard:pending`, then\",\"Create the issue with `ard:scanner:<name>` plus the route's label (`ard:pending` by default), then\")\nsub(\"It closes scanner issues still at `ard:pending` with no activity\",\"It closes scanner issues still at `ard:pending` with no activity (issues filed under `route: none` or `needs-human` lack `ard:pending` and are never candidates; #204 may widen this)\")\nsub(\"the job gets `ard:needs-human`.\",\"the job gets `ard:needs-human`. `redact.gitleaks.block_autoclose_when_missing` (default false) is read by the scanner guard, which runs the same pass over findings: when set and gitleaks cannot run, scanner autoclose stops for that run too.\")\nsub(\"Anything unset takes its default:\",\"Scanners also take `route` (`pending`, `none` or `needs-human`). Anything unset takes its default:\")\nopen(f,'w').write(s)\nE\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; git diff --stat | tail -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2722,"cache_read_input_tokens":87422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2722},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a1a7d6-7fdc-45ac-9b6e-7e6bb020d70e","uuid":"13ac7cf7-5403-4ec8-870d-0079bfbc38b4","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:49:01.078Z","request_id":"req_011ChLHG883oymcqrput2Tuw"}
