{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLHMkXCBLN2ZAEE88WE1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Issue #215 is implemented: scanners now have a `route` key, and every scan passes through a pre-filing secret guard that can't be turned off. `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` pass, but I didn't run `make lint`, so only gofmt and vet were checked.\n\n- **`route`:** it takes `pending` (the default for executable scanners), `none` (the default for LLM scanners) or `needs-human`. A bad value, `pending` on an LLM scanner, or `route` on a non-scanner role is a config error. The route decides the labels on new issues, on the dry-run synthetic issue and on joins. An existing issue is only joined when its `ard:` labels are exactly the scanner label plus the route label.\n- **Guard:** `internal/scanner/guard.go` scans the title, fingerprint, group, files and body of every finding. It checks them with the builtin scanner and the controller's known secret values, and also with gitleaks when that is enabled. It runs after the scan and before the diff, in dry-run too.\n- **Guard hit:** a hit, or a builtin-pass failure, records `scan_failed` and changes nothing. Logs name only the rule and field, never the text.\n- **Gitleaks failure:** if gitleaks is enabled but can't run, nothing is filed or joined, but autoclose of fully-gone issues still happens. The new `redact.gitleaks.block_autoclose_when_missing` key (default false) turns that off.\n- **Stale closer:** I did not add a `stale_test.go` run test. The existing `TestDecide` rows already show that issues filed under `none` or `needs-human` are never stale-closed.\n- **Gitleaks fixture check:** it runs inside `TestFixturesPassTheGuard` when `ARD_GITLEAKS_BIN` is set, not as a separate integration-tagged file. I didn't run it here.\n\nI also updated `docs/proposal.md` for the guard, route, backpressure, grouping, filing, stale closer, gitleaks and config text. The report is in `.ard/215/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":92318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1094},"output_tokens":690,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72a1a7d6-7fdc-45ac-9b6e-7e6bb020d70e","uuid":"0619d2a8-156b-4570-9f24-b9771f6beac9","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:50:13.285Z","request_id":"req_011ChLHMkLmmHrQi59dAbRQD"}
